# EtherCAT setup notes

## This branch (feature/iod-elc-kernel-transport)

Plant controller binary: **`iod-elc`** with kernel module **`elc_ethercat`**.

Generic guidance (repo):

- **`etc/README.md`** — quick start for config layout
- `TRANSPORT.md` — elc install, RT params, rates
- `scripts/iod-elc.sh` — load `elc_ethercat`, run `iod-elc`
- `etc/elc_topology.conf` — default topology (`ELC_TOPOLOGY_CONFIG` overrides)
- `etc/recipes/` — sample servo CoE setup listings
- `/opt/etherlab-cyclic-kmod` — transport source (DKMS, library, tools)

Site-specific LPC, plugins, and service units live in **your plant tree**. Point
`scripts/iod-elc.sh` at those paths via argv/env.

```bash
./scripts/iod-elc.sh --name MYCELL /path/to/plant/lib /path/to/plant/config
```

Do **not** use IgH `ec_master` / `scripts/ethercat.sh` for iod on this branch
(`scripts/ethercat.sh` and `scripts/etherlab.sh` only print that message).

## Legacy IgH userland (other branches only)

`iod_sdo` / ecrt lives on **`prod-experimental-mqtt-fix`** (and related prod lines).
Those checkouts may still use IgH master packages or `../ethercat/` source.

See also: `iod/docs/LEGACY_ECRT_REMOVAL_PLAN.md`.
